# Second run (kept as evidence, not edited): CI job 113424162076 (p19-reminder-v2-16), commit a8170894.
# 14 of 16 PASS again; both browser cases stopped with P19M_FIXTURE_TARGET_NOT_LISTED, now with the stored row:
# the target's PRODUCTION_GAP condition is ACTIVE on page 0, ord 1. So the first run's "race" reading was wrong.
# Cause (a product defect in the screen): parseConditionsPage compared the server's echo of the query with
# JSON.stringify. The server returns the query as jsonb, whose keys come back in jsonb's own order (limit, state,
# offset, run_id, rule_id), so every real page was refused and no list was drawn; the unit fixture echoed the
# client's own object, which hid it. The settle check passed on an absent list.
# Fix: the echo is compared key by key (exact keys, equal values); a unit test uses the jsonb order. All 70 real
# reminder v2 replies recorded from the native cases (LOCAL_PG16_DEV, not evidence) now pass the screen's parsers;
# before the fix the 10 condition pages were refused and every other reply passed. The browser script now stops
# with the panel's own error text and requires the list to exist.
